      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kannon K. Shanmugam",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1229",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2df2a4b59c805b80c01a8b548c9455ea6e96f564d1d6e47d89f5a17cea539fb3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2df2a4b59c80-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the America Invents Act, Congress transformed the nation's patent laws. As part of its shift from a first-to-invent to a first-to-file system, Congress revised the definition of \"prior art\" and clarified the proper understanding of the phrase \"on sale.\" The on-sale bar, like the other bars in the definition, reaches only a disclosure that makes the claimed invention available to the public."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1229",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2df2a4b59c805b80c01a8b548c9455ea6e96f564d1d6e47d89f5a17cea539fb3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2df2a4b59c80-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Isn't it always the case that if you offer it to even one person or to a small group of people, it's on sale?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1229",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2df2a4b59c805b80c01a8b548c9455ea6e96f564d1d6e47d89f5a17cea539fb3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2df2a4b59c80-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So is that right? If -- if -- if you assume for a moment that the law was pretty settled before the AIA, then do you think that the AIA would -- that the language added in the AIA would have been capable of flipping that settled law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1229",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2df2a4b59c805b80c01a8b548c9455ea6e96f564d1d6e47d89f5a17cea539fb3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2df2a4b59c80-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the invention is patented or described in a printed publication, that means that the inventive idea has been made available to persons skilled in the art such that they would be able to make it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1229",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2df2a4b59c805b80c01a8b548c9455ea6e96f564d1d6e47d89f5a17cea539fb3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2df2a4b59c80-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In other words, can I"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jay",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1229",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2df2a4b59c805b80c01a8b548c9455ea6e96f564d1d6e47d89f5a17cea539fb3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2df2a4b59c80-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think so -- I think you can."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1229",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2df2a4b59c805b80c01a8b548c9455ea6e96f564d1d6e47d89f5a17cea539fb3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2df2a4b59c80-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But given your position -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "government",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1229",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2df2a4b59c805b80c01a8b548c9455ea6e96f564d1d6e47d89f5a17cea539fb3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2df2a4b59c80-0002-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government's amicus brief in this case is entitled to respectful consideration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1229",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2df2a4b59c805b80c01a8b548c9455ea6e96f564d1d6e47d89f5a17cea539fb3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2df2a4b59c80-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
